---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy | Pigeon DNA Testing';
const description = 'How SENO Biotech collects, uses, shares, transfers and protects personal and testing data for racing-pigeon DNA, pathogen and kinship testing, and your privacy rights.';

const hreflang = [
  { lang: 'en', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/en/privacy-policy/' },
  { lang: 'zh-CN', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/yinsi/' },
  { lang: 'x-default', href: 'https://senopigeon.com/yinsi/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description} lang="en" canonical="/en/privacy-policy/" {hreflang}>
  <Header />

  <main id="main">

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-900 to-brand-700 py-16 text-white">
    <div class="container-x">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-brand-100">Effective date: 25 November 2025 &nbsp;|&nbsp; Last updated: 24 November 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-x py-16">
    <div class="prose prose-gray mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Zhangjiakou SENO Biotech Co., Ltd. (“SENO Biotech”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses, stores, shares and protects personal information and testing data when you visit senopigeon.com, request a quotation, order a test, submit a sample or communicate with our team.</p>

      <p>We provide animal-use molecular testing for racing-pigeon breeders, lofts, distributors, veterinarians and research partners. We do not provide human medical diagnosis and our services are not directed to minors. Please read this Policy before using the site or our services; if you do not agree, please do not use them.</p>

      <h2>1. Controller, scope and contact details</h2>
      <p>The controller of your personal information and testing data is Zhangjiakou SENO Biotech Co., Ltd. This Policy covers this website, email and phone/WeChat communications, sample intake, laboratory testing, report delivery and after-sales support.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Company: Zhangjiakou SENO Biotech Co., Ltd.</li>
        <li>Registered address: Building 3, North Silicon Valley, Qiaodong District, Zhangjiakou, Hebei, China</li>
        <li>Website: https://senopigeon.com</li>
        <li>Privacy contact: martin@senobiocorp.com (subject line: “Privacy Request”)</li>
        <li>Phone | WeChat: +86 15612372623</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where applicable law requires an EU representative, we will update the representative details on this page. Until then, you may still contact us using the details above and we will handle your request under applicable law. This Policy is not legal advice.</p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <h3>2.1 Website and technical data</h3>
      <p>Our hosting and security providers may automatically record IP address, browser and device type, access time, requested page, referring page, language preference and security-event logs. We use this information to deliver pages, prevent abuse, diagnose faults and keep the site secure.</p>
      <p>This is currently a static website. We do not operate comments, user accounts, a login area or visitor uploads, and we do not collect information for those features. If we add them, we will update this Policy first and explain the relevant processing.</p>

      <h3>2.2 Enquiries, orders and fulfilment</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Identity and contact data: name, title, email, phone/WeChat, country or region and shipping address.</li>
        <li>Order data: service type (flight-gene, pathogen, DNA ID/kinship or kits), quantity, quotation, invoice, payment status and tracking number.</li>
        <li>Communications: enquiries, support requests and complaints sent by email, phone/WeChat or other channels.</li>
        <li>Distributor/partner data: company name, contact person, business qualifications, territory and settlement details.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2.3 Sample and testing data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Sample data: sample ID, species/breed, sample type (feather, blood card, oral/cloacal swab), collection date, shipping information and sample condition.</li>
        <li>Testing data: nucleic-acid extraction, qPCR/STR results, quality-control records, genotype or pathogen interpretation, report versions and re-test records.</li>
        <li>Context you provide: pigeon ring number, pedigree, race record, clinical signs or epidemiological information used to interpret or review results.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Pigeon samples are not human genetic samples, but they are still sensitive business and testing data. We do not use them for human medical purposes or for unrelated commercial promotion without authorisation.</p>

      <h3>2.4 Payment and financial data</h3>
      <p>We may record payment method, payment status, invoice details, tax number and bank-transfer reference. Full card numbers and PayPal passwords are handled by the payment provider; we do not store full card numbers or payment passwords on this website.</p>

      <h2>3. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
      <p>We process personal information only where we have a lawful basis:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contract:</strong> to accept orders, process samples, perform tests, issue reports and arrange shipping and after-sales service.</li>
        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> where required for a specific purpose (for example optional marketing or uses beyond the service); you may withdraw consent at any time.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> tax, accounting, import/export, biosecurity, market-regulation, judicial or regulatory requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> protecting the website and laboratory, preventing fraud and abuse, improving quality and conducting anonymised statistics and research, where your rights are not overridden.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal claims:</strong> establishing, exercising or defending legal claims.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where applicable law requires separate consent for sensitive information, we will ask for it separately and will not bundle it with the service.</p>

      <h2>4. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>This is primarily a static site. Our hosting and security provider may use essential security cookies or similar technologies (for example, to distinguish normal visitors from automated attacks). We currently do not use advertising cookies, cross-site behavioural tracking or third-party marketing pixels. If we introduce analytics or advertising tools, we will update this Policy, provide any required notice and obtain consent where required.</p>
      <p>You can delete or block cookies in your browser. Blocking essential cookies may affect security checks or parts of the site.</p>

      <h2>5. Sharing, processors and disclosure</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information or test results. We share data only as needed to provide the service and with appropriate safeguards:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Laboratory and quality staff:</strong> personnel who handle samples and testing data for testing, review and report authorisation.</li>
        <li><strong>Logistics and customs providers:</strong> recipients and shipment data needed to send samples/kits, clear customs and track delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment and finance providers:</strong> payment, refund, invoicing and account reconciliation.</li>
        <li><strong>Hosting, email and IT providers:</strong> page hosting, security, email delivery, backup and system maintenance.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional advisers:</strong> lawyers, accountants, insurers or compliance advisers where necessary.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal and regulatory authorities:</strong> where required by law, court order, regulator or biosecurity rules, or in an emergency to protect human or animal health.</li>
        <li><strong>Business transfer:</strong> in a merger, reorganisation or asset sale, data may transfer as part of the transaction; we will require the recipient to continue to protect it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Processors may act only on our instructions and must maintain confidentiality and security. Cross-border transfers are addressed in section 6.</p>

      <h2>6. International transfers</h2>
      <p>Laboratory testing is primarily performed in China. The website is delivered through global hosting and security providers such as Cloudflare, so access logs, email and technical-support data may be processed outside China. International logistics, payment and communication providers may also involve overseas recipients.</p>
      <p>Where we transfer personal information internationally, we will use measures required by applicable law, such as separate consent, data-processing/transfer agreements, security assessments or other lawful mechanisms. You may ask us for information about these safeguards, except where disclosure is prohibited by law.</p>

      <h2>7. Retention</h2>
      <p>We retain information only as long as needed for the purposes described, unless a longer period is required by law:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Orders, reports and QC records:</strong> normally 5 years from report delivery for re-testing, after-sales support, quality traceability and legal defence.</li>
        <li><strong>Finance, invoice and tax records:</strong> as required by applicable accounting and tax law (normally at least 10 years).</li>
        <li><strong>Samples:</strong> unless the order, a written agreement or law provides otherwise, samples are kept for 30 days after report delivery for necessary re-testing or disputes, then inactivated/disposed of under biosample procedures.</li>
        <li><strong>Enquiries and support records:</strong> normally 2 years; complaints and dispute records are kept for a reasonable period after resolution.</li>
        <li><strong>Website security logs:</strong> normally 90 days, unless extended to investigate a security incident.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>When a period ends, we delete or anonymise the data. Where backup, legal hold or technical constraints prevent immediate deletion, we restrict access and continue to protect it.</p>

      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>We use physical, technical and organisational measures appropriate to the risk, including role-based access, authentication, encrypted transmission, laboratory zoning, sample-ID segregation, backups, staff confidentiality training and incident response. No internet transmission or storage is completely secure. If a breach may affect your rights, we will notify regulators and affected individuals as required by law.</p>

      <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to applicable law, you may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>request access to and a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information;</li>
        <li>ask us to delete information that is no longer necessary (except where retention is required by law);</li>
        <li>withdraw consent, restrict or object to certain processing;</li>
        <li>request portability of information you provided, where technically feasible and required by law;</li>
        <li>complain to a supervisory authority or ask us to explain our processing rules.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Send requests to martin@senobiocorp.com with the subject “Privacy Request”. To protect data, we may verify your identity and your relationship to the sample/order. We normally respond within 15 business days; complex requests may take longer with an explanation. Legal exceptions (such as the rights of others, legal holds or trade secrets) may apply.</p>

      <h2>10. Minors</h2>
      <p>The site and services are intended for adult customers with full legal capacity and are not directed to minors. We do not knowingly collect minors’ personal information; if we learn that we have done so, we will delete it promptly.</p>

      <h2>11. Third-party links and sub-sites</h2>
      <p>The site may link to genetics, health, research, payment or logistics pages operated by third parties. Those sites have their own privacy policies; we are not responsible for their processing. Please read the relevant policy before submitting information.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this Policy to reflect changes in our services, law or technology. Material changes will be flagged on the site or through order communications. The updated version applies from the effective date shown on the page.</p>

      <h2>13. Contact and complaints</h2>
      <p>For questions about this Policy, our processing or your rights, contact Zhangjiakou SENO Biotech Co., Ltd., martin@senobiocorp.com, Phone | WeChat +86 15612372623, Building 3, North Silicon Valley, Qiaodong District, Zhangjiakou, Hebei, China. You may also complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>

      <h2>14. Language versions</h2>
      <p>This Policy is available in Chinese and English. The two versions are intended to express the same rules; if they differ, the Chinese version prevails, except where mandatory local law provides otherwise.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

    </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
